1. Introduction
The Ultrasonic Radar Scanner is an Arduino‑based system that simulates the behavior of a real radar unit by sweeping an ultrasonic sensor across a defined angle range and measuring distances in real time. A servo motor rotates the sensor, while an LCD1602 display shows the current angle and detected distance. This project demonstrates core embedded‑systems concepts such as sensor integration, servo control, timing, and real‑time data visualization.
